  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual &amp; reproductive Health - district support - SRH District</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Specific Objective health for BARAME project on SRH is to ensure accessible, evidence-based, improved and innovative health services (with a special attention to sexual and reproductive health services) with increased citizens&#x2019; participation and engagement in development.   The orientations from the Belgian side are fully in line with the Rwandan policies and strategies, in particular the Rwandan Health Sector Strategic Plan IV (HSSP 4), Reproductive Maternal Newborn Child and Adolescent Health Policy 2017-2030 (RMNCAH), Maternal Newborn child health strategic plan 2018-2024 (MNCH) and Family Planning/Adolescent Sexual Reproductive Health and Right strategic plan 2018-2024 (FP/ASRHR) which have adopted &#x2018;the Life Course Approach&#x2019;.  In brief, the focus in health sector is designed to ensure that all women, newborns, children, adolescents and men have universal access to quality integrated Reproductive, Maternal, Newborn, Child and Adolescent Health and Family Planning services. BARAME uses a project approach, specifically focusing on priority bottlenecks identified at operational level in 7 districts (6 rural, 1 urban). The Sexual &amp; Reproductive Health. district support project (SRH District) is a collaboration between Enabel and the Rwandan government, funded by the BTC Operations Fund. This project falls under the sector of Population &amp; Reproductive Health. Reproductive health care, which is part of the broader top sector of Population &amp; reproductive health (13xxx). The project&apos;s inception was prompted by a legal agreement between Belgium and Rwanda, with the aim to improve access to quality integrated Reproductive, Maternal, New-born, Child, and Adolescent Health (RMNCAH) services for all women, new-borns, children, adolescents, and men in Rwanda. The project scope includes district support, with a focus on enhancing sustainable and resilient urban development in the districts of Rubavu, Musanze, and Rwamagana, as well as promoting inclusive economic development. A steering committee will be established for each sector to oversee the implementation of objectives and interventions, ensuring strategic guidance, validating work plans, financial plans, operations, and financial reports.</narrative>
  </description>
